text:
priya: Noticed a fairness issue in the JS SDK leaky-bucket prefill. When running multi-tenant sampleapp benchmarks, one tenant's prefetches drain the shared credit window and other tenants get hard-throttled. Repro in staging.

nolan: Yikes. Do you have quick repro steps?

priya: Yes: 1) start sampleapp with shared bucket mode (default) 2) tenant A: prefetch=3, high QPS 3) tenant B: steady low QPS 4) run load for 2m. Tenant B hits repeated 429s despite low usage.

priya: Logs snippet from gateway:```
WARN credits: tenant=tenantB balance=-12 reserve=0 prefill_consumed=18
INFO credits: tenant=tenantA balance=+4 prefetch_reserved=20
```

sam: How is prefill accounted today? I thought prefetch reservations decrement a global token count, then expire after X ms.

nolan: That's the plan but the JS impl does two things wrong: 1) it charges prefetch reservations synchronously before confirming cursor validity, so old prefetches can hold credit, 2) it uses a single shared window without per-tenant soft limits.

priya: Exactly. Also saw an edge where retries double-dip: a prefetch that errors will retry and re-reserve credit without releasing first.

ops-eli: Can you paste the minimal failing code path?

priya: Here is the snippet from sdk-js (simplified):
```js
// bad: reserve before spawn
if (bucket.reserve(prefetchCost)) {
  spawnPrefetch(cursor);
}

// retry path also calls reserve again on error
```

nolan: Proposed fixes: A) move reserve to inside the worker after validating cursor version B) make reserve atomic (reserveIfNotStale(cursorVersion)) C) add per-tenant soft-window with shared fallback.

sam: I like A+B as fast fixes. C is a larger policy change but probably needed for multi-tenant fairness.

eve: For quick mitigation we could also cap prefetch_reserve_per_tenant to 5% of window by default. That gives breathing room.

priya: I prototyped a patch that: 1) defers reserve until after cursor check, 2) uses CAS on reservation to avoid double-reserving during retry, and 3) emits telemetry `credit_drift` and `prefetch_reserve_failures`. Local staging looked much better.

priya: Patch excerpt:```js
// worker loop
if (cursorStillCurrent(job.cursor)) {
  if (bucket.reserveIf(cursor.id, prefetchCost)) {
    doFetch(job);
  } else {
    metrics.increment('prefetch_reserve_failures')
  }
} else {
  metrics.increment('prefetch_cursor_mismatch')
}
```

ops-eli: Nice. Add a guard in the retry handler to ensure reservations are released in any error path. Also instrument a histogram `reserve_hold_ms` so we can detect long-held reservations.

nolan: We should also add a small integration that runs two tenants simultaneously in staging and asserts max imbalance < 10% over 2m.

sam: Agree. Can we do a short-term config toggle for customers: `sdk.prefetch_per_tenant_cap` and default it to 0 (off) but enable in our canary? That avoids shipping policy change to everyone.

priya: I'll open a PR with the changes + tests + a sampleapp canary config. Draft: https://github.com/redwood-inference/sampleapp/pull/2468 (WIP). The PR includes unit tests simulating concurrent prefetch + retry.

devex-bot: Issue created: #5399-client-credit-drift-prefetch-fairness (assigned to nolan) https://issues.redwood.ai/5399

eve: For telemetry, add `tenant_balance` gauge and an alert if any tenant's balance < -50 for > 1m. That should catch regressions early.

ops-eli: Canary plan: enable patch in staging for 1h with `prefetch_per_tenant_cap=5%` and `reserve_hold_abort_ms=1000`. Abort if `credit_drift` rate > 0.5% of requests.

nolan: I'll own the canary run and add the integration test. ETA for PR review: tomorrow AM.

sam: After merge, we should add a short devex note under onboarding: "If using multi-tenant workloads, enable per-tenant prefetch caps or upgrade SDK to avoid cross-tenant credit drift."

priya: Sounds good. I'll include the doc blurb in the PR. Logs and perf dumps attached in the issue.

eve: Thanks team. Catching this early saved a customer lane for sure. :thumbsup:
